/*Q26. Write a Java program to implement a Product Price Comparison System using a static nested class, constructor, and instance method.
The provided ProductPriceComparison class must contain a static nested class named Product.
Product class
Declare the following private instance variables:
• productId (String): stores the product ID.
• name (String): stores the product name.
• price (double): stores the product price.
Constructor
Implement a parameterized constructor Product(String productId, String name, double price) to initialize all three instance variables using
the this keyword.
Method
Implement comparePrice(double otherPrice) in the Product class. Compare the product's price with otherPrice and display:
• "Cheaper" if the product price is less than otherPrice .
• "Expensive" if the product price is greater than otherPrice .
• "Same Price" if both prices are equal.
The ProductPriceComparison class must implement main() to perform the following operations:
1. Read the product ID, product name, product price, and comparison price.
2. Create a Productobject using the constructor.
35 Call comparePrice() with the comparison price.
Input Format:
• The first line contains a string representing the product id.
• The second line contains a string representing the product name.
• The fourth line contains a floating-point number representing the other price to compare with.
Output Format:
• Print one of the following based on the price comparison:
Cheaper
Expensive
Same Price
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class ProductPriceComparison {
 
    static class Product {
        private String productId;
        private String name;
        private double price;
 
        Product(String productId, String name, double price) {
            this.productId = productId;
            this.name = name;
            this.price = price;
        }
 
        void comparePrice(double otherPrice) {
            if (price < otherPrice) System.out.println("Cheaper");
            else if (price > otherPrice) System.out.println("Expensive");
            else System.out.println("Same Price");
        }
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String id = sc.nextLine().trim();
        String name = sc.nextLine().trim();
        double price = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        double other = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
        Product p = new Product(id, name, price);
        p.comparePrice(other);
        sc.close();
    }
}
